    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "CAMBRIDGE"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 104,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 137.333, 483.333, 195.667, 502.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "Languageon themove"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 107,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 138.333, 389.667, 209.0, 482.333 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Cairns (Your View, 3 January) is mistaken in his interpretation of English words. In the UK, “stations”are where passengers wait for their trains, buses and trams; a “depot”is where buses are parked and serviced, while a “shed”is where trams and railway locomotives are parked. DAVIDRWILLIAMS"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 123,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 138.667, 375.333, 204.0, 390.667 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "DAVIDR WILLIAMS LLANDUDNO; CONWY"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 125,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 137.667, 268.0, 208.667, 369.0 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "I agree entirely with Ken Smith and Neil Cairns’ comments about the misuse of English words. The most annoying phrase I hear is “See you later”when parting from temporary company, especially when there is no chance of the speaker and oneself ever meeting “later”! It may seem friendly but it is a pointless remark. One other word which"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 137,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 138.0, 240.333, 208.0, 269.333 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "is, to me, disrespectful is the word “cops”instead of police. DAVIDCULM"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 141,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 139.0, 233.667, 176.333, 240.333 ],
