    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "DAVID CULM"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 143,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 138.667, 218.667, 179.333, 226.667 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "DERBYSHIRE"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 145,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 139.0, 197.667, 197.333, 212.0 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Can I brieﬂy add two more Americanisms"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 91,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 217.333, 575.0, 288.333, 654.0 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "My two least favourite examples of Americanisms are “from the get-go”in place of the simpler “from the start”, and worst of all “stepping up to the plate”, a baseball-related term. We are a cricketing nation – we “step up to the crease”surely? DAVIDDAY ANDOVER, HAMPSHIRE"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 95,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 218.0, 567.333, 288.0, 575.333 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "ANDOVER; HAMPSHIRE"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 97,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 216.667, 502.667, 287.0, 560.333 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "It’s not an Americanism (or is it?) but can someone explain the term “hike”as in “rail fare hike”? Is it different in some way to “rail fare increase”? It’s beginning to be irritating. KATHYWEBSTER"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 105,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 217.667, 497.0, 269.0, 503.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "KATHY WEBSTER"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 106,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 217.333, 482.0, 272.667, 497.333 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "LEAMINGTON SPA WARWICKSHIRE"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 109,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 216.667, 403.333, 289.333, 475.333 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Could I ask why the word “cupcake”appears to have replaced “bun”? “Bun”is shorter than “cake”, thus signifying the fact that buns are smaller than cakes, whereas “cupcake” is almost twice as big and has no logical connection with cups. TJHONEYBONE"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 119,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 217.333, 396.667, 265.333, 404.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "TJHONEYBONE"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
